## 1. Why Choose Cypress?

Cypress ek next-generation front-end testing tool hai jo modern web applications ke liye banaya gaya hai. Selenium ki tarah isme complex driver setup nahi karna padta kyunki ye seedhe browser loop ke andar execute hota hai.

---

## 2. Installation & Setup

Apne project folder mein Cypress ko install karein:

```bash
npm install cypress --save-dev
```

Cypress Test Runner ko open karne ke liye command run karein:

```bash
npx cypress open
```

---

## 3. Writing Your First E2E Test

`cypress/e2e/home.cy.js` file banayein aur ye test code likhein:

```javascript
describe('DevLearn Home Page Test', () => {
  it('successfully loads and searches tutorials', () => {
    cy.visit('http://localhost:3000');
    cy.contains('Learn. Build. Grow.').should('be.visible');
    cy.get('input[placeholder*="Search"]').type('React{enter}');
    cy.url().should('include', '/search');
  });
});
```

---

## 4. Running Tests in Cypress GUI

Cypress interactive dashboard mein real-time DOM snapshots, time-travel debugging aur network stubbing provide karta hai jisse flaky tests ko instantly debug kiya ja sakta hai.
